From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: cubie-a7s: let the eMMC run HS400 with enhanced strobe

WHY
---
`mmc-sunxi-stop-claiming-the-controller-cannot-do-enhanced-strobe` implemented ->hs400_enhanced_strobe and stopped the probe from masking
MMC_CAP2_HS400_ES out, and then nothing happened: the board DT never said
mmc-hs400-enhanced-strobe, so the core kept selecting plain HS400 and the
implementation only ever ran as a negative control. That is the proof debt
`mmc-sunxi-stop-claiming-the-controller-cannot-do-enhanced-strobe` carries, and this property is what closes it.

The reason to want the mode is not throughput, it is determinism. In plain
HS400 the card's CMD responses are sampled with the controller's clock, so the
response path depends on a sampling delay. With enhanced strobe the card
returns them framed by the data strobe it sends with the data, and the
controller samples them off that strobe.

WHERE THE VALUES COME FROM
--------------------------
Card, read on the 8 GiB board 2026-09-19:
  EXT_CSD[184] STROBE_SUPPORT = 0x01   the card offers it
  EXT_CSD[196] DEVICE_TYPE    = 0x57   HS400-1.8V among the rest

Controller, A733 UM 11.3.8.41: SMHC_CQE_CTRL (0x1A0) bit [8] DS_SAMP_RESP_EN
(enables response sampling on the data strobe). Searched end to end in V0.92 and V1.00:
that bit is the only place the manual mentions an enhanced strobe. No general
enable exists, and no CQE has to be running for it -- the bit lives in the CQE
control register, which is a placement, not a dependency. `mmc-sunxi-stop-claiming-the-controller-cannot-do-enhanced-strobe`'s header carries
that reading.

Core, drivers/mmc/core/:
  host.c:399               parses the property -> MMC_CAP2_HS400_ES
  mmc.c mmc_select_card_type()  offers HS400ES only with caps2 && strobe_support
                           && HS400 available
  mmc.c mmc_select_hs400es()    HS -> bus width 8 with EXT_CSD_BUS_WIDTH_STROBE
                           -> HS400 -> ios.enhanced_strobe = true ->
                           host->ops->hs400_enhanced_strobe()

WHAT IT CHANGES
---------------
One property in the mmc2 node. The switch sequence changes with it: HS400ES
goes HS -> DDR-8bit-with-strobe -> HS400 and never passes through HS200, so
HS200 tuning does not run on the way in.

WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM
----------------------
- No throughput claim. The strobe frames the response, not the payload, and
  the read side is already at 324 MB/s decimal against the part's stated 300.
- It does NOT remove the data-strobe sweep from init. mmc_init_card() calls
  ->execute_hs400_tuning for an hs400es card as well (mmc.c:1848), so `mmc-sunxi-tune-the-sample-delay-instead-of-running-it-at-zero`'s
  sweep still runs and still decides DS_DL. Whether that sweep should exist at
  all is a separate question and a separate patch.
- It is not a fix for the DS_DL problem: a DS_DL of 21 wedges a sustained read today, and
  nothing here changes which delay the sweep lands on.

VERIFIED / NOT VERIFIED
-----------------------
- Applies clean at fuzz 0 on a fresh unpack with the series in order: yes.
- dtc: the decompiled dtb must carry mmc-hs400-enhanced-strobe in the mmc2
  node -- checked on the built dtb, not asserted here.
- Silicon: NOT proven. The observable, on the 8 GiB board:
    * dmesg names HS400ES, not HS400 -- the core's own timing string, and
      ios.enhanced_strobe = 1
    * SMHC_CQE_CTRL (0x0402_21A0) reads bit 8 set while the card is up
    * a 2 GiB sequential read and write verify clean (verify_bad = 0) at the
      rates plain HS400 gives today: read ~309 MiB/s, write ~140 MiB/s
  What falsifies it: the card fails to switch (mmc_select_hs400es reports an
  error and init falls back or fails), or the bit does not read back set,
  which would mean the CQE control register needs the CQE block powered.

ISSUE
-----
The `mmc-sunxi-stop-claiming-the-controller-cannot-do-enhanced-strobe` proof debt of that patch; the determinism half of the
HS400 goal.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -906,6 +906,43 @@
 			mmc-hs400-1_8v;
 
 			/*
+			 * Enhanced Strobe. With it the card returns CMD
+			 * responses framed by the data strobe instead of by
+			 * the controller's sampling clock, so the response
+			 * path stops depending on a delay that was chosen at
+			 * runtime.
+			 *
+			 * Card side, measured on the 8 GiB board (2026-09-19): EXT_CSD[184]
+			 * STROBE_SUPPORT = 0x01, and EXT_CSD[196] DEVICE_TYPE
+			 * = 0x57 already carries HS400-1.8V. The core needs
+			 * both plus the host cap before it offers HS400ES
+			 * (drivers/mmc/core/mmc.c, mmc_select_card_type():
+			 * caps2 & MMC_CAP2_HS400_ES && strobe_support &&
+			 * avail_type & EXT_CSD_CARD_TYPE_HS400).
+			 *
+			 * Controller side: SMHC_CQE_CTRL[8] DS_SAMP_RESP_EN,
+			 * (data-strobe response sampling enable, A733 UM
+			 * 11.3.8.41) -- the only place the manual mentions an
+			 * enhanced strobe at all. `mmc-sunxi-stop-claiming-the-controller-cannot-do-enhanced-strobe` implements
+			 * ->hs400_enhanced_strobe and writes exactly that bit;
+			 * without this property it never ran positively, which
+			 * is the proof debt this closes.
+			 *
+			 * Reader for the property: drivers/mmc/core/host.c:399
+			 * -> MMC_CAP2_HS400_ES.
+			 *
+			 * ⚠ This does NOT remove the data-strobe sweep from
+			 * init. mmc_init_card() calls ->execute_hs400_tuning
+			 * for an hs400es card too (drivers/mmc/core/mmc.c:1848),
+			 * so `mmc-sunxi-tune-the-sample-delay-instead-of-running-it-at-zero`'s sweep still runs and still decides DS_DL.
+			 * What changes is the response path and the switch
+			 * sequence: hs400es goes HS -> DDR-8bit-with-strobe ->
+			 * HS400 without the HS200 stage and without HS200
+			 * tuning.
+			 */
+			mmc-hs400-enhanced-strobe;
+
+			/*
 			 * Soldered eMMC at footprint U8A. ⚠ The schematic
 			 * symbol carries KLM8G1GETF-B041 (V1.10 p9); the part
 			 * actually fitted on the 8 GiB board is a SanDisk iNAND
